'''Yonezawa Balboa, S.A.''' is a Balboan subsidiary of [[Yonezawa Motors]] (Okaiken) that operates a {{w|completely knocked down|CKD}} vehicle assembly facility in the [[Portnou]]. The company assembles several Yonezawa passenger vehicle models — including sedans, hatchbacks, and SUVs — from imported kits, primarily for the domestic Balboan market and for export within the [[BTPMEU]] tariff area.

The subsidiary was established in 2003 to take advantage of the BTPMEU's preferential tariff treatment for vehicles assembled within the economic union. The facility receives {{w|completely knocked down|CKD kits}} from Yonezawa Motors' plants in Okaiken, performing body welding, painting, and final assembly operations. Approximately 60 per cent of output is sold domestically, with the remainder exported to BTPMEU member states.

Yonezawa Balboa is the largest single CKD operation in the country, with annual output of approximately 18,000 vehicles. The company is not separately listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]], as it is wholly owned by its parent.

